{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0001874178","cik":"0001874178","slug":"rivian-automotive-inc-de-874178","name":"Rivian Automotive, Inc. / DE","ticker":"RIVN","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Motor Vehicles & Passenger Car Bodies","sic":"3711","country":"CA","website":"","listed_years":4.3,"first_annual":"2022-03-31","last_filing":"2026-07-30","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001874178&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Rivian Automotive, Inc. / DE files with the SEC under \"Motor Vehicles & Passenger Car Bodies\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 4 years.","It reported $5.9bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 27.2% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 10.8%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 17 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 27.2% year on year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025), reaching $1.7bn in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 7 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from -15.8% to 10.8% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"Net cash of $866.0m against total assets of $15.1bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 37.0% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"Gross margin is only 10.8%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-50.4% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"About 17 months of cash at the current burn ($5.3bn against $3.7bn a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000035/0001874178-26-000035-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000035"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 14.7% over the year (Q2 2026 vs Q2 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000187417826000054/0001874178-26-000054-index.htm","accession":"0001874178-26-000054"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.2% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1874178/000206649126000011/0002066491-26-000011-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 3.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.03,"consecutive":2,"current":0.108,"current_display":"10.8%","threshold_display":"3.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 12.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.12,"consecutive":2,"current":0.272,"current_display":"27.2%","threshold_display":"12.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":17.311,"current_display":"17 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 22.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.22,"consecutive":1,"current":0.147,"current_display":"14.7%","threshold_display":"22.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"leverage_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Debt to equity rises above 1.30","metric":"debt_to_equity","comparison":"abo